ROOT CAUSE (durable finding): OCR pipeline has a heavy CPU-bound prep stage (render@300DPI + grayscale preprocess + classify) BEFORE the GPU OCR stage. When N workers all land on fresh volumes at once they preprocess in LOCKSTEP and saturate CPU. At 4 workers the 5090 CPU hit ~91-94% and per-worker prep throughput COLLAPSED ~10x (50->5 pg/min/worker), indefinitely starving the GPU. The 4th worker is NET-NEGATIVE on prep-heavy volumes (1920s multi-vol chapter PDFs, 1500-3270 pg each). 3 workers leaves enough CPU headroom that a worker reaches the GPU stage promptly.

