  (GPUs idle entire window -> prep-phase numbers, NOT OCR-load numbers. No >80C, no OOM, no instability ever.)

OOM/HANG: None. No OOM either box (5080 OCR model only ~1-5GB VRAM, 16GB ample). No true hang - prep kept advancing, just pathologically slow under contention. All worker bumps/kills/restarts clean (taskkill /F /T).

RECOMMENDATION: Stay at 3/1. To measure a real 4/2 OCR rate you'd need to defeat prep lockstep (pre-render volumes, or separate CPU prep pool feeding a GPU OCR pool) or test on a box with more CPU cores. As-is, the 4th worker on the 5090 hurts.
